.TH DEXPIRESCORING 8
.SH NAME
dexpirescoring \- Diablo program to age the dreaderd cache scoring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dexpirescoring
[
.B \-H
.I halflife
]
[
.B \-v
]
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
When
.B readercache
is on, dreaderd counts per group how many articles are read, how many of
those reads were cache hits, and how many new articles arrive.  The counts
are kept in cache.hits (path_cachehits, normally /news/cache.hits) and
decide which groups' articles are worth caching.
.PP
.I dexpirescoring
updates the count of new articles of every group in the reader's
dactive.kp and, with
.BR \-H ,
ages all counts so that recent reading weighs more than old reading:
each count is divided by
.RI 2^( elapsed / halflife ),
where
.I elapsed
is the time since the last aging run.  Run it from cron, for example
daily.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-H " halflife"
Halve the counts every \fIhalflife\fP seconds of elapsed time.  Without
it the counts are not aged.
.TP
.B \-v
Print each group's counts: reads, cache hit percentage, new articles and
the read/new ratio.
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /news/cache.hits
the scoring file (path_cachehits).
.TP
.I /news/dactive.kp
the reader's active file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dexpirescoring -H 604800 -v
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
dreaderd(8),
dexpirecache(8),
diablo-files(5)
